id "q-338686/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7305bc72-5483-59d9-b9ab-ed5490df93ab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338686/field-3/992b7eba006d2e9dbc5164a70da2c7d6ad1516ef9c596fff2442c25469b6c9ec" :answer-field/choices ["q-338686/field-3/1028b50c0cbb7a1b02cf8d6690d1353e6705478818994ba94f4b73db89dd35ba" "q-338686/field-3/a80f87583a7638a8cfa7e07097c9287040410a5efd3bcfa8f3adf36eee1a57d5" "q-338686/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-338686/field-3/ffeba10a45a48637eba90b6793acca00a17ca7ef374e72c96214cf6199cae1b9" "q-338686/field-3/992b7eba006d2e9dbc5164a70da2c7d6ad1516ef9c596fff2442c25469b6c9ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/field-4/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" :answer/id #uuid "f1e8f728-51d4-582e-bab2-f17180b7ed20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/field-4/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" :answer/id #uuid "d1ed7ac2-6ab5-508c-b60c-dacbd7b6f49d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/field-4/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :answer/id #uuid "fd666ab4-8745-5418-ac64-cb03a8791d56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "fec5e295-18c4-5434-80ab-8be83bcc0ab5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338686/field-4/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :answer-field/choices ["q-338686/field-4/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" "q-338686/field-4/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" "q-338686/field-4/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686" :question/id #uuid "2dbc0eba-24a7-50e0-964f-4c8949e5821f" :question/math-academy-id "q-338686" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0,\\,y(0)=y(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(0) & {y}_{2}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Dirichlet boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=1,{\\beta }_{i}=0,a=0,$ and $b=1,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(0) & {y}_{2}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-m-2 & =0 \\\\ (m-2)(m+1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=2$ and $m=-1,$ and so the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}\\text{ and }{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ {e}^{2} & {e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={e}^{-1}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{3}}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338686/field-1" "q-338686/field-2" "q-338686/field-3" "q-338686/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d9576e0-3be5-5d05-8cc8-c3ecde496b46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339097/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer/id #uuid "604e5c8a-54be-5d79-a1e2-9bf13da6ff21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339097/field-1/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" :answer/id #uuid "5d83d14e-80f2-50e8-a64e-30a6a2b20d18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339097/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5db0bdb-da71-52eb-bb19-e556b6d71abb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339097/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer-field/choices ["q-339097/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" "q-339097/fiel