892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-339176/field-3/83513287b1d7c1593e2cf389df7cf451bc86d0ee3f484ee0acb6ae8276afbca1" "q-339176/field-3/9f24afa9df43f72c3a914e78e20cff5680f4634ea38dc639a8b1de2805f80ddc" "q-339176/field-3/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" "q-339176/field-3/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-339176/field-3/c45a4d0b2872fcda13fabf8b8eea12e28c70d90d420a04f9d49f0f10d85c0a30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339176/field-4/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" :answer/id #uuid "468ab820-f7f2-58a1-983d-c283f1d4decf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339176/field-4/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" :answer/id #uuid "6ba4ff4e-c0af-5574-bcf0-e8fca7773130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339176/field-4/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :answer/id #uuid "bb3e8fd3-8f3b-591f-9b29-4d40c7164892" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339176/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c42f11fc-ae5d-5551-896f-cdeca7e9eb82" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339176/field-4/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-339176/field-4/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" "q-339176/field-4/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" "q-339176/field-4/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339176" :question/id #uuid "355bfeb1-d0b8-53cd-b763-3f92856140f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-339176" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4y=0,\\,2y(0)-{y}^{′}(0)=2y(1)-{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have mixed (Robin) boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=2,$ ${\\beta }_{i}=-1,$ $a=0,$ and $b=1,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (m-2)(m+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=2$ and $m=-2,$ and so the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}\\text{ and }{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=-2{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4{e}^{-2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =0(4{e}^{-2})-0(4) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=0$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has infinitely many solutions }.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339176/field-1" "q-339176/field-2" "q-339176/field-3" "q-339176/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d9576e0-3be5-5d05-8cc8-c3ecde496b46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339176"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338980/field-1/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" :answer/id #uuid "93d6aefc-013e-5c57-906a-69b94b46c801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338980/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer/id #uuid "97b5eb50-f677-5075-8a8d-901968baaac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338980/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eaac056c-4b06-59da-ac6b-5e1f0aa4f8d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338980/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer-field/choices ["q-338980/field-1/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" "q-338980/field-1/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79d